  "title": "The Next Mini Cooper Could Be Rear-Wheel Drive",
  "summary": "The city-friendly Mini has changed a lot since the original model made its debut in 1959: It has gradually gotten bigger, quicker, and headed more upmarket. It has never strayed from its pioneering front-wheel-drive roots, however, but that could change in the next couple of years. The next Mini Cooper might share a rear-wheel-drive platform […]",
